[gd_scene format=3]

; The Sounding, east of the Mere (map offset (340.5, -79)): a sonar chapel on the lake shore, where the machines
; listened to the deep. Its great bell hangs over a sounding well of black water. The pilgrim drops into the well (its
; walls are too high to climb back) and floats to a shelf at the waterline: the Ballast relic. With it, the only way on
; is down: sink to the well's floor, under the wall, and rise in the shaft beyond, into the chapel's east hall (a
; shrine), then up the ringers' plinth, over the shaft onto the wall, and over the well's mouth to the door.

